    id: "lore.oldbab.house",
    scope: OLD_BAB,
    topics: [{ aim: "household-home" }, { aim: "remember-dead" }, { occasion: "day.mend-home" }],
    evidence: "documented",
    title: "Family vaults under the floor in Ur",
    text: "Leonard Woolley excavated a whole Old Babylonian neighbourhood at Ur: courtyard houses of mud brick on baked-brick footings, with rooms opening onto a central court, stairs to the roof where people slept in summer, and in many a small chapel at the back. Beneath the chapel lay a brick vault where the family's dead were laid, one after another over generations. The dead stayed at home and were given food and water in the kispum rite each month. Houses were divided among sons at their father's death, the eldest often taking an extra share, and deeds show them sliced into ever-smaller parts.",
    wiki: ["Ur", "Leonard Woolley", "Architecture of Mesopotamia"],
