    evidence: "documented",
    title: "The Old Woman and her rituals",
    text: "Hittite archives preserve dozens of healing and purification rituals, many credited to named practitioners, most often a woman called the 'Old Woman', written with the Sumerian signs MUNUS ŠU.GI. She was a professional: called to cure illness, impotence, family quarrels or bad dreams, she worked with wool, dough figurines, puppies, piglets and running water, transferring the evil into an object and carrying it away. Her rituals are written as step-by-step instructions, with the words to say, sometimes in Luwian or Hurrian. Some rituals were also for births, and midwives worked with birthing stools and incantations to the mother goddesses.",
