    text: "Reliefs from Sennacherib's palace at Nineveh show how the great winged bulls, lamassu, weighing up to 30 tonnes, were moved. At the quarry at Balatai they were roughed out, then lashed to wooden sledges and dragged over rollers by gangs of hundreds pulling on ropes, with levers behind, overseers with sticks, and the king watching from a chariot. On the river they went on rafts buoyed by inflated skins. The workers were mostly deportees from conquered lands, Chaldeans, Arameans and others, set to building work. Assyria moved perhaps millions of people across its empire, using them as labour and settlers.",
