    scope: OTTOMAN,
    topics: [{ goal: "news" }, { goal: "neighbour" }, { occasion: "day.linger" }],
    evidence: "documented",
    title: "News and backgammon in the coffeehouse",
    text: "Coffeehouses opened in Istanbul in the 1550s and within a generation were everywhere in the Ottoman lands. Men of all ranks sat on benches along the walls, drinking coffee, smoking pipes, playing backgammon and chess, listening to a meddah storyteller or a poet, and above all talking. It was where news was heard and passed on, where janissaries and guildsmen met, and where rumours about the sultan started, which is why sultans repeatedly tried to close them. Clerics condemned coffee as an intoxicant and a novelty; the argument was lost. Women drank coffee at home and in the hammam, and it became part of every visit and betrothal.",
