    scope: WAR_FAMINE,
    topics: [{ aim: "restore-household" }, { occasion: "day.check-store" }, { goal: "food-store" }],
    evidence: "documented",
    title: "The famine years of the First World War",
    text: "The First World War brought famine to much of West Asia. In Mount Lebanon and Syria, an Allied blockade, Ottoman requisitions of grain and animals for the army, a locust plague in 1915 and hoarding killed perhaps a third or more of the mountain's people between 1915 and 1918; survivors remembered eating grass and carob husks, and children dying in the streets of Beirut. In Iran, occupied by Russian, British and Ottoman armies, crop failure and requisition caused the famine of 1917 to 1919, with a death toll put in the hundreds of thousands at least, and more by some estimates. Families survived by selling land, emigrating, or sending children to relatives.",
